---
description: How the standalone Swift test harness works
globs: Tests/**/*.swift,test.sh,Sources/Hilal/*.swift
alwaysApply: false
---

- Tests don't use XCTest or `swift test`. `test.sh` compiles each test file with `swiftc` against an explicit source list and runs the binary.
- `TimingTests.swift` compiles with only `Timing.swift`. `BehaviorTests.swift` compiles with `Timing, Preferences, PrayerService, Reminders, NotificationService, Model`. `Hilal.swift` (macOS UI, `@main`) is excluded.
- When a new source file becomes a dependency of `Store` or the helpers, add it to the matching `swiftc` line in `test.sh`.
- Add behavior cases as `try await test("name") { ... }` using `check(condition, "message")` (precondition-based: the first failure aborts the run).
- Use the existing fakes (`FakeLoader`, `FakeReminders`), fixture helpers, an isolated `UserDefaults` suite, and an injected `now`; never touch real notifications, location, or `.standard` defaults.
- Network checks belong only in `liveChecks()` behind `--live`.
